      "audience": {
        "@type": "BusinessAudience",
        "name": "Irish farmers and agricultural businesses"
      },
      "description": "Farm solar PV designed around agricultural loads including milking, milk cooling, ventilation, cold storage, grain drying and water pumping. Typical payback 2-4.5 years. Two grant routes: the SEAI route at 20-25%, which as of September 2026 is the practical option for most farms, and TAMS 3 at up to 60% for solar PV up to 62 kWp and battery storage up to 31 kWh with a EUR 90,000 ceiling, which has become difficult to secure. Local Power is registered with both the SEAI and the Department of Agriculture and advises on which route is genuinely achievable. Accelerated capital allowances apply on either route."
